WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.137
Now we are ready to run the complete clinic schema
This is

00:00:05.164 --> 00:00:10.864
an instructor-guided reference not a script you need
to memorize Before

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:15.604
clicking Run scan the script and count the CREATE
TABLE statements Then

00:00:15.630 --> 00:00:20.590
look for primary keys unique business identifiers
foreign keys and check constraints

00:00:22.419 --> 00:00:26.366
Run the schema in the browser and confirm that
PostgreSQL creates the

00:00:26.379 --> 00:00:32.211
tables successfully The order matters because parent
tables need to exist

00:00:32.224 --> 00:00:37.454
before child tables can reference them If you copy
the script into

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:42.640
pgAdmin use it as a reading exercise Trace each
foreign key back

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:47.095
to its parent table The main goal is to see how the

00:00:47.122 --> 00:00:51.635
conceptual and logical design decisions become
executable PostgreSQL
